{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games","id":174225,"title":"Changeling ideas from pop culture and video games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T09:50:46-07:00","id":174225,"title":"Changeling ideas from pop culture and video games","content":"So I want to make a changeling based off of a video game character. Specifically Link from the Legend of Zelda series. My idea is that this changeling would be the epitome of the iconic 'The Hero' TV Trope, specifically with leanings toward the character of Link, the Hero of Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2875-jamesfhj","name":"JamesFHJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T07:03:27-07:00","id":175219,"title":"","content":"Link is only the Hero of Time in Ocarina of Time. That said, I'd make him a Wizened Soldier, Link is dexterous but never talks. Blade Lore also fits, though I'd make it actually stack with other specializations, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T11:52:33-07:00","id":175454,"title":"","content":"Hoping I haven't misinterpreted your thread idea here, James. I'm looking at running a Lovecraft-inspired Changeling game (see my<i> Arkham Lost </i>thread) that draws less from classic folklore and more from cosmic horror tropes. Pledges and noble orders fall aside, in favor of mutation, subtle corruption, mental illness, unholy breeding, and the craving for knowledge that should not be known. I'm setting it in Arkham, with a focus on Miskatonic University, and loving how it's come out so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:18:09-07:00","id":175503,"title":"","content":"Nope. Not misinterpreted at all.<br /> <br /> Proindrakenzol::.. That was my first thought too, but Wizened doesn't seem right to me. Fairest feels more like the iconic hero. Handsome, as well as capable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2875-jamesfhj","name":"JamesFHJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T16:02:08-07:00","id":175621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JamesFHJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=175503#post175503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Not misinterpreted at all. Proindrakenzol::.. That was my first thought too, but Wizened doesn't seem right to me. Fairest feels more like the iconic hero. Handsome, as well as capable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that just isn't Link. Link isn't super social (he doesn't talk) and he does any shit job people throw jis way. He even matches one of the siggested appearances: thin with elfin features. If you'd rather make him fairest it's your character, but to me Link is a Wizened Soldier. There are other Heros you could use: Hercules could be an Ogre, Captain America could be a Fairest Dragon, Batman a Darkling, and many others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T16:10:07-07:00","id":175626,"title":"","content":"Lady Gaga and Katy Perry screams to be changelings. Or Others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","user":"Baroqo","date":".  Grammar 06-20-2014, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T18:15:01-07:00","id":175665,"title":"","content":"The nightmare sequence from Hugo is an excellent representation for a durance of a mechanical elemental kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T18:41:46-07:00","id":175667,"title":"","content":"Alan Wake (including the American Nightmare expansion) manages to pretty much nail many of the themes and moods of Changeling, I feel. Everything about it, from the narrative-driven nature of the monster and its obvious bane towards light, to Alan's time beneath the lake being a perfect example of a durance, to Mr Scratch and his shadow powers being the perfect example of a murderous Fetch, combines to give me a terrifically strong Changeling feel the entire business. There's even a conspicuously large amount of time spent running around shadow-infested forests that give me a pretty strong Hedge-vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T23:05:15-07:00","id":176766,"title":"","content":"Take Changeling, and in lieu of existing in a setting with any of the other WoD splats, stick it in the world of Neil Gaiman's Sandman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T16:13:23-07:00","id":177407,"title":"","content":"Are there any other <i>Homestuck </i>readers who play Changeling? I'm fascinated by the idea of incorporating some Homestuck stuff into Changeling, it feels very thematically appropriate in some ways. Doc Scratch could basically be thought of and the Handmaid's &quot;Keeper&quot; (which could be taken in an interesting direction considering that the effectively omnipotent scratch was a mere puppet of something greater the whole time...) and the chronicle setting I'm building right now includes an Autumn Oracle modeled pretty heavily after Terezi Pyrope.<br /> I'd imagine that at least a few of the SBURB lands could serve as inspiration for a Durance as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T16:43:28-07:00","id":177434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=175626#post175626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lady Gaga and Katy Perry screams to be changelings. Or Others.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about their managers?<br /> I always thought it would be a funny direction to take a Changeling chronicle to follow one of those &quot;alt-tween&quot; bands or musicians: create some NPCs blatantly parodying Jeffree Star, Brokencyde, Fall Out Boy, whoever...one of those musicians who targets the preteen audience with material meant to be shocking to their parents and make the kids feel like rebels.<br /> <br /> Showcase an NPC who is a parent getting into some strife with their kid and blaming it on &quot;that awful music she's listening to-you can call me old-fashioned, but when I was her age at least the music targeted at us wasn't <i>that </i>explicit.&quot; Showcase a young NPC, maybe a little cousin of one of the PCs, getting more and more introverted, wearing more and more all-black band merchandise with...weird symbols on it, symbols that raise the hair on the back of the local Autumn Courtier's neck. They start acting more and more alien, distant from their peers and the adults around them, eventually ending friendships with the kids who don't listen to the same music they do-they were all &quot;posers,&quot; or they &quot;didn't really care about me,&quot; or the age old and eternally popular: &quot;They just didn't understand me.&quot; This culminates when the band or artist comes to town and holds a concert which ends disastrously: dozens or hundreds of preteens dead or missing, and the ones that survive come out acting like completely different people than they were even before listening to this music: Angrier, nastier, even more destructive and alienated.<br /> <br /> The mortal explanation, of course, is some faulty wiring that burned out at the exact wrong moment and led to a catastrophic accident, or perhaps a drug slipped to a lot of concert-goers by some unknown person that caused a mass bad trip, and a lot of press releases are made and the band's name is on the front page of the news every day for weeks. What really happened (unless the PCs were given an opportunity to stop it that they took) was this: During the culmination of the set, a gateway to Arcadia was opened right there in the middle of the theater, and the brainwashed youth were easily herded through it, certain that this was the way to a world where they would be understood and appreciated as they weren't at home. The Faeries got as many fetches made to replace the taken children as possible, but even if a Fae lord had the resources to make so many duplicates of so many humans, it would grow bored with the task quickly: Thus, many of the children are declared dead or &quot;missing&quot; as no replacement for them emerged or the one that did was so shoddy and unstable that it collapsed in on itself within hours of appearing in the mortal world.<br /> <br /> If the PCs couldn't stop this, they obviously have a responsibility to stop it from happening again, and so they go after the musician/musicians...only to find that there's nothing supernatural about the musician themself. They're a puppet, a mortal Glamour-junkie, and that whatever <i>did </i>plan for the deaths and disappearances of all those children wears a business suit, is nowhere near the tour bus they've just stormed, and has gained power not only from the lives it's just stolen but from the grief and rage and other emotions being broadcast (even amplified) worldwide by the endless media coverage of this tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T06:15:03-07:00","id":179618,"title":"","content":"While watching &quot;Gankutsuou: The Count of Monte Cristo&quot; (an anime adaptation of &quot;The Count of Monte Cristo&quot; set in the 51st century including mechas and aliens and the titular count is possessed by a vengeance demon called Gankutsuou), I felt that this would work quite well as a Changeling story. I haven't read the original novel, so most of my knowledge of the story is from the anime.<br /> <br /> Edmond Dantes, instead of being sent off to some prison somewhere, his rivals manage to send him to Arcadia. Or he actually is accused of a crime he didn't commit and sent to prison and while there, he is taken by the True Fae. I also considered the possibility of replacing Fernand Mondego's role in the story, the man who marries Edmond's old lover Mercedes, with a fetch of Edmond (this works if his rivals send him directly to Arcadia, but if he is sent to prison first his fetch would probably still be there).<br /> <br /> While in Arcadia, he encounters Gankutsuou, the king of the cavern (or Gankutsuou might be his keeper). If Gankutsuou is the keeper, he releases him because he thinks this whole vengeance-thing will probably be amusing. If he isn't, then he probably helps Edmond escape somehow.<br /> <br /> Edmond Dantes returns to the human world, using his changeling powers to hide his true identity, and calls himself the Count of Monte Cristo, secretly plotting his revenge on those who sent him away and took his life from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/941-sahrimnir","name":"Sahrimnir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T08:09:36-07:00","id":179717,"title":"","content":"One of my players decided that his Keeper, instead of making the traditional Fairy-tale land, wanted a realm that was basically every noir movie rolled into one psychosphere. Result? Said character looks and talks like Humphrey Bogart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:53:55-07:00","id":179861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=175621#post175621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that just isn't Link. Link isn't super social (he doesn't talk) and he does any shit job people throw jis way. He even matches one of the siggested appearances: thin with elfin features. If you'd rather make him fairest it's your character, but to me Link is a Wizened Soldier. There are other Heros you could use: Hercules could be an Ogre, Captain America could be a Fairest Dragon, Batman a Darkling, and many others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Link may not be talk much, but you can not deny that something about him is incredibly attractive and charismatic. Hell, Link is 1 step away from having his own fan girl club. Saria, Malon, Ruto, those dancers in Majora's Mask, Midna. Everywhere Link goes, he seems to charm the ladies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, Link does actually talk, when you're given the option to say Yes or No to certain dialogue in the game. Plus characters respond to Link as if he told them information.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Link was a Fairest, I'd say he should be a Minstrel, since the majority of his games involve some form of musical instrument","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T21:19:32-07:00","id":181628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foolish Milex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=176766#post176766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take Changeling, and in lieu of existing in a setting with any of the other WoD splats, stick it in the world of Neil Gaiman's Sandman.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the very first thing i ever thought when reading changeling for the first time, anything neil gaiman really,even American gods can give you a feel for how changelings are disconnected yet attached to the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1951-themoetan","name":"TheMoetan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T02:40:23-07:00","id":181787,"title":"","content":"Anyone played The Wolf Among Us? It's about, ooh, 90% how a struggling Changeling freehold feels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T06:18:07-07:00","id":187000,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://namesakecomic.com\" target=\"_blank\">Namesake</a> provides some possibilities that could be adapted as \u201cworlds of fiction as Arcadian Realms\u201d, with the Namesakes being abductees who were chosen strictly because of their names, and whose durances resemble famous fairy tales. The oddest feature is the introduction of Writers, mortals connected to the newly-returned Namesakes who wield a storycrafting magic and serve as stabilizers for the newly-returned Namesakes.<br /> <br /> Namesake thus far has provided examples of changeling durances (including an example of a faerie creature mutating a hapless mortal to help her survive the faerieland she found herself in), a fetch, and most recently a Goblin Market (or at least something that\u2019s <i>called</i> a goblin market).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-03-2014, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T18:32:31-07:00","id":187562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=187000#post187000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://namesakecomic.com\" target=\"_blank\">Namesake</a> provides some possibilities that could be adapted as \u201cworlds of fiction as Arcadian Realms\u201d, with the Namesakes being abductees who were chosen strictly because of their names, and whose durances resemble famous fairy tales. The oddest feature is the introduction of Writers, mortals connected to the newly-returned Namesakes who wield a storycrafting magic and serve as stabilizers for the newly-returned Namesakes.<br /> <br /> Namesake thus far has provided examples of changeling durances (including an example of a faerie creature mutating a hapless mortal to help her survive the faerieland she found herself in), a fetch, and most recently a Goblin Market (or at least something that\u2019s <i>called</i> a goblin market).</div> </div> </div> </div>And I just read through the whole archive in one sitting. Thanks for the tip! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/941-sahrimnir","name":"Sahrimnir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T21:13:54-07:00","id":187664,"title":"","content":"Spirited Away would need very few changes to work great as a Durance in Arcadia. It's a reminder that the Gentry don't necessarily need to steal anyone away: lay out food where mortals can stumble on it and they'll be all too happy to make pigs of themselves (Chihiro's parents to Beasts), while their daughter gives up her name and memories as she sells herself into service (Chihiro to Wizened) at the bathhouse for the Gentry, operated by a greedy and powerful proprietress (Yubaba). Perhaps the girl might have faded away entirely (or at least into a Darkling), and forgotten herself for still longer, had she not gotten assistance from an older Changeling (Haku as a Fairest, likely Dual-Kithed Draconic and Waterborn, and possible Loyalist for a time). Zenibaba could be a rival Gentry to Yubaba, engaged in a subtle war over that realm, with No Face as either a more powerful Darkling or a weaker Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T21:43:38-07:00","id":189181,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of Anime, Fullmetal Alchemist would make for an excellent Changeling chronicle. Depending on which of the two Anime adaptations you use, it could be fun either way as well. (If you went for the original adaptation, the entire thing is clearly set in the hedge, with the final ending revealing the real world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> I mean, consider how the story starts - Two brothers make a fell bargain to bring their mother back to life and trade their bodies for it. Can't imagine how appealing that deal would be to True Fae. Then followed by a life-long pledge to recover their bodies and discover the truth. The incarnations of the seven deadly sins - clearly Fae Actors and horrible dread beasts ruled by their vice, near invulnerable, but also determined. And then there's the alchemy in the world - &quot;equivalent exchange&quot;, a contract with the world to trade one for another. Except when you cheat.<br /> <br /> Heck, this writes itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T03:37:01-07:00","id":192227,"title":"","content":"RWBY's protagonists have some interesting seasonal motifs that fit well into kiths. The Snowskin Weiss feeds off the sorrow of her family's slaves; she remembers an Arcadia of chill hallways and hollow, massive knights. When Ruby, a Flowering, expends Glamour, ghostly rose petals dance around her. For Yang, it's flames- burning in her eyes and hair as she vents her wrath on Fae lackeys. Blake, a graceful Whisperwisp, harvests fear from those who would subjugate her people once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T08:32:07-07:00","id":194641,"title":"","content":"Having re-watched <i>Wreck It Ralph</i> the other day, I was struck by how Changeling-like the protagonists (Tron-like computer programs) are.<br /> <br /> Ralph is clearly an Ogre of some kind, Felix is a Wizened repairman, the various racing characters in Sugar Rush could be Wizened racers, or perhaps some sort of sickeningly-cute Fairest ...<br /> <br /> It's an interesting take on how Keepers need not be in Actor form - Realms and even Wisps can create Changelings as well. The fun-yet-brutal lives of the game characters, bound to serve the shadowy giants behind the screen or be unplugged forever, would be a great Durance for a PC sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:12:18-07:00","id":195996,"title":"","content":"Hellboy 2: The Golden Army is so similar to Changeling I wouldn't be surprised if the writers actually play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2904-stonepedal1","name":"stonepedal1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:43:46-07:00","id":196018,"title":"","content":"<i>The Dresden Files</i>, while ostensibly about a mage, involve so many amazing Fae. Later in the series more time is spent in Arcadia, and with it comes more and more ideas for characters, durances, and most of all Keepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T21:53:35-07:00","id":202645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/174225-changeling-ideas-from-pop-culture-and-video-games?p=196018#post196018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Dresden Files</i>, while ostensibly about a mage, involve so many amazing Fae. Later in the series more time is spent in Arcadia, and with it comes more and more ideas for characters, durances, and most of all Keepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought Molly's capture and rescue in Proven Guilty made for an excellent Snowskin origin story. And the White Court would make awesome Fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T06:50:04-07:00","id":292934,"title":"","content":"If Keepers are aping narratives found in human culture, than maybe at some point there may be Klingon Kiths, just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}